      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A key early landmark was the Mono Inn, established in 1922 as a bunkhouse and restaurant, which helped attract settlers and travelers to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mono_city_california",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mono City's early growth tied to late‑19th‑century mining and ranching booms that swept the Mono Basin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mono_city_california",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Volcanic eruptions and repeated Sierra Nevada glaciations have carved moraines that shape Mono City's basin hydrology.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mono_city_california",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Mono City's economy centers on retirement living, seasonal tourism drawn by Mono Lake's tufa formations and bird habitat, and the historic Mono Inn.",
